{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795288574,"nonce":"O3dFdrn/qyPE+WwS7z9qiu5vobQ=","message":"Landed on the branch gerfunkt: the conversion in commits 627e9d4 to 8598082 before the rebase and now up to commit 8598082, and the client in commit 9bbad0b.\n\n- cargo xtask models reads assets/planes/planes.toml, converts each FBX file with a reader in Rust, turns and scales the model to the plane of the rules, cuts it along the five parts, and writes web/assets/planes/\u003ckey\u003e.glb. cargo xtask build and serve run it first.\n- The WWI fighter has 1,636 triangles: fuselage 604, left wing 200, right wing 215, tail 128, engine 489. The file is 3.2 MB, almost all of it the texture of 2048 by 2048 pixels.\n- The client draws each plane from the five meshes, with a light tint for each pilot. A broken part disappears. A screenshot of a solo match shows the model.\n- A pilot flies the last model of the list whose kills the pilot has reached. Only one model exists, so every pilot flies it. A second model on the asset branch needs one entry in the manifest.\n\n**Limits that stay.**\n\n- The wings of this model sit about 2 m ahead of the wing boxes of the rules, so a shot from the side at the visible wing can miss the part of the rules. The hit shapes of the rules do not follow the model.\n- The engine cut splits the wheel, and it takes a thin strip of the upper wing.\n- The manifest records the author and the service from the branch and the file. The prompt and the licence terms are not recorded: the artist must add them before the game ships.\n- The cut leaves each part open where it was cut.\n\n**Ruling: the FBX reader is own code of about 200 lines.** Why: the crates for FBX had no release since 2022. Cost if wrong: a later model with pivots or concave polygons needs a fix in the reader.\n\nThis issue stays open for the second model and for the hit shapes.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}